{"item_id":"feed:/resources/materials/physical-vapor-deposition/","version_id":"fcf9079ad45657e09903d78c29d7b8ae301b4348d9c2d777777b5d1e831378a0","decision":"reject","reason":"Although fresh, this is a general manufacturing-process explainer rather than evidence about frontier AI for 3D modeling, CAD, or intelligent physical systems. It offers no AI capability claim, geometry-verification result, or simulation-ready workflow relevant to the publication's lead topics.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:/resources/materials/recrystallization-of-metals/","version_id":"ded55799bfd57b9e786dbfccb038115b95d469ba2c6a470457c0869c6e17bd6c","decision":"reject","reason":"The dated passage is a conventional metallurgy overview, not a development in AI-assisted CAD, 3D modeling, robotics, or verification. Its material-science content does not supply a checkable frontier-model capability or a decision-relevant product development.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:/resources/supply-chain/oil-refinery/","version_id":"03628944819a5390db2f0c3005cb2bcb336118528a4d5c646d7dfe25c82500ea","decision":"reject","reason":"This fresh article describes refinery operations but has no stated connection to AI-native 3D modeling, CAD, simulation assets, or robotics verification. It is outside the publication's relevance criteria and supplies no claim whose supporting check bears on those topics.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","decision":"accept","reason":"This is fresh CAD-industry coverage of Autodesk University announcements, including a next-generation Autodesk Assistant and AI work in Forma and Fusion, and is relevant commercial context for CAD teams. The excerpt reports Autodesk's conference message rather than an independently checked capability result, so its claims should be treated as vendor-announcement claims; this trade report is not independent corroboration of Autodesk's underlying announcements. It also adds commercial perspective, though practitioner and customer evidence remain missing.","piece_ids":["01","03"]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","decision":"accept","reason":"This fresh research-oriented survey directly addresses frontier models for 3D modeling, computational design, and robotics, and its passage identifies both progress and the unresolved need to confirm tolerances and manufacturability. Its stated check is a live collection and verification of 1,646 public posts and accompanying benchmark evaluations across 707 cases, which supports using it to examine evidence rather than treating its conclusions as proof of every capability. The excerpt does not disclose the verification protocol, graders, or task conditions, so its aggregate findings require scrutiny and leave practitioner perspective missing.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
{"item_id":"youtube:4dbaTrlaLJ8","version_id":"b92f49a0aeaa5497e59c4087239e6125670fea5992a0c80ba51d2162575d7ffa","decision":"defer","reason":"The newly published NVIDIA session is relevant robotics context because Newton concerns robot simulation and OpenUSD-based assets, but the supplied automatic transcript only promises a walkthrough of new functionality. It gives no timestamped demonstration, settings, reproducible benchmark, or physical-transfer check, so the claimed improvements cannot yet be evaluated under the core test. Audio-backed timestamps and concrete evidence of what the simulator verified would settle this.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"youtube:Lnex2Q9bpvQ","version_id":"2d7286605286a5ff73bbb89d48b506a026e1112723a7ff7534475c34e4e5f48e","decision":"reject","reason":"The short is fresh and CAD-relevant, but it is a tutorial describing existing Onshape custom features rather than a novel AI or frontier-CAD development. Its claim that custom features can speed workflows is not accompanied by conditions, measurements, or a checkable comparison, and it does not meet the novelty criterion.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"youtube:jLndwlduyzc","version_id":"a3209c32c4153b9ba8b68c0b0d0fc493c4e67807292a91e91e6e5a2c9c2cd938","decision":"reject","reason":"This is a fresh practitioner tutorial about robust parametric modeling, but the excerpt presents established Onshape techniques rather than a new frontier-model capability or AI-native product development. Its robustness claims are instructional assertions without stated test cases, failure rates, or independently inspectable checks, so it lacks the novelty and evidence needed for selection.","piece_ids":[]}
